2. BrainWeb simulated brain images (not the authors' work)

The synthetic demonstration sessions in dummy_data/ (the conformed volumes brain.mgz and the segmentations
aseg.mgz, the PNG slices in slice_cache/) and the demonstration volumes in alzheimer-xai-cdss/public/demo/ are
derived from the BrainWeb: Simulated Brain Database (McConnell Brain Imaging Centre, Montreal Neurological
Institute, McGill University, https://brainweb.bic.mni.mcgill.ca/), 20 normal anatomical models, simulated T1.

- These images are not the work of the authors of this repository, and the authors do not claim them as their
  own. The authors only processed them (skull stripping and segmentation with FastSurfer, slicing, conforming).
- The license of this repository (PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0) does not cover them. The BrainWeb site states no
  license or redistribution terms and asks only that its references be cited in any published work that uses
  the data.
- The original BrainWeb files are not included; tools/make_brainweb_demo.py downloads them from BrainWeb.
- The authors will remove these derived files on request of the rights holders.

