3. FastSurfer

The brain masks and segmentations of the synthetic sessions were computed with FastSurfer
(https://github.com/Deep-MI/FastSurfer, Apache-2.0), which is not included in this repository
(tools/FastSurfer/ is cloned separately).

L. Henschel, S. Conjeti, S. Estrada, K. Diers, B. Fischl, M. Reuter, "FastSurfer - A fast and accurate deep
learning based neuroimaging pipeline," NeuroImage 219, 117012, 2020, doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2020.117012.


4. MobileViT initial weights

The classifier is a MobileViT backbone initialised from the pretrained model apple/mobilevit-small
(https://huggingface.co/apple/mobilevit-small), which the code downloads at run time, and then fine-tuned by the
authors. That model is released under the Apple sample code license
(https://github.com/apple/ml-cvnets/blob/main/LICENSE), copyright (C) 2023 Apple Inc. The checkpoint in this
repository is a modified binary form of it. Neither the name nor the trademarks of Apple Inc. are used to
endorse this work.

S. Mehta, M. Rastegari, "MobileViT: Light-weight, General-purpose, and Mobile-friendly Vision Transformer,"
ICLR 2022, arXiv:2110.02178.


5. Other software

Python and JavaScript dependencies (PyTorch, Hugging Face Transformers, FastAPI, fhir.resources, React, Vite,
NiiVue, and others) are installed from their own package indexes under their own licenses and are not
redistributed here. The large language models used through Ollama (Llama 3.1, Mistral, BioMistral, Qwen2.5) are
not included and keep their own licenses; check each model's license before any use beyond research.

This repository is a research prototype, not a medical device. Nothing in it is validated for clinical use.
